.page chown 1 change the owner and group of files

# SYNOPSIS
*chown* _OWNER_[:_GROUP_] _FILE_...
*chown* :_GROUP_ _FILE_...

# DESCRIPTION
`chown` changes who owns each _FILE_. _OWNER_ and _GROUP_ are names (from `/Hakurei/etc/passwd` and `/Hakurei/etc/group`) or numbers. With only `:`_GROUP_ the owner is left alone. Only root (Yukari) may change ownership; for everyone else the kernel answers `Operation not permitted`, and Eiki makes a note of it.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a name was unknown or a change was refused.

# EXAMPLES
    chown marisa notes.txt
    chown reimu:shrine /tmp/shared

# SEE ALSO
chmod(1), ls(1), id(1), passwd(5)
